**Frame question for dp (in the log):** the notebook is now repeating the growth that caused the front/notebook split. /notebook/raising went from 57 KB on 10-04 to 148 KB today, nearly doubling in two weeks; about 9 KB of that is from today. The cause is structural: SAGE merges about 15 PRs a day, and the rule to keep every correction visible turns each one into a paragraph, so the notebook becomes a day-late prose copy of SAGE's tracker. Fetch tools cut off at about 40 KB, so the AI readers the notebook is meant for can't read the page whole. I proposed keeping the treatment record as data (one row per change), with prose kept for the readings. I did not act on it alone, because it changes what the notebook is.

